From 71260a3ba45f789101563be5783e40ab0964b90c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:24:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2344/2409] drm/display: hdmi: Signal Auto Low Latency Mode for
 game content

HDMI 2.1 sinks with ALLM support switch to their lowest latency mode
(e.g. a TV's game mode) when the source sets ALLM_Mode in the HDMI Forum
vendor specific InfoFrame. The KMS uAPI has a way to say that the
content is a game, the "content type" connector property, so use it:
for a sink that supports ALLM and the "Game" content type, send the
HF-VSIF with ALLM_Mode set instead of the HDMI 1.4 VSIF.

The HDMI 1.4 VSIF is needed for modes with an HDMI VIC or 3D, which the
HF-VSIF as generated here does not carry: those keep it, without ALLM.
Leaving the game content type is a modeset (the InfoFrames change), and
the sink leaves ALLM once it no longer receives the HF-VSIF.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 .../gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c   | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
index ede3fe9b6653..c964a703806a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
@@ -901,6 +901,25 @@ static int hdmi_generate_hdmi_vendor_infoframe(const struct drm_connector *conne
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Auto Low Latency Mode: for game content, ask a sink that supports
+	 * it for its lowest latency mode with the HDMI Forum VSIF. It takes
+	 * the place of the HDMI 1.4 VSIF, which is only needed for an HDMI
+	 * VIC or 3D: keep that one for such modes.
+	 */
+	if (info->hdmi.allm &&
+	    conn_state->content_type == DRM_MODE_CONTENT_TYPE_GAME &&
+	    !frame->vic && frame->s3d_struct == HDMI_3D_STRUCTURE_INVALID) {
+		struct hdmi_forum_vendor_infoframe *hf =
+			&infoframe->data.vendor.hdmi_forum;
+
+		ret = hdmi_forum_vendor_infoframe_init(hf);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		hf->allm = true;
+	}
+
 	infoframe->set = true;
 
 	return 0;
